# Test-fixture boards used as INPUT by tests/ - keep tracked despite the broad
# output patterns above (test_bga_fanout_summary, test_diff_pair_route).
!/kicad_files/interf_u_unrouted_placed.kicad_pcb
!/kicad_files/routed_output.kicad_pcb

# Sibling PROJECTS that are spec, not output. `/kicad_files/*kicad_pro` above
# exists because the chain drops a .kicad_pro next to every board it writes,
# and six such files were once committed for boards that are generated and
# ignored. These are the opposite case: the DRC floor a real board declares,
# for a board that is itself tracked. Without them the board grades at the
# toolchain's fallback 0.25/0.55 rather than its own rules (#441), and
# test_457_fresh_clone_fixtures already enforces the invariant that makes
# this safe -- a tracked project must have a tracked board.
!/kicad_files/watchy.kicad_pro
!/kicad_files/tigard.kicad_pro

